{
  "title": "Adjectives",
  "note": "Adjectives agree with their noun in gender, number and case; most use first- and second-declension endings: ἀγαθός, ἀγαθή, ἀγαθόν. After the article an adjective is attributive: ὁ ἀγαθὸς λόγος or ὁ λόγος ὁ ἀγαθός, 'the good word'. Outside the article it is a predicate: ἀγαθὸς ὁ λόγος, 'the word is good'. Some adjectives use one form for masculine and feminine: αἰώνιος.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Dickinson College Commentaries, Greek Core Vocabulary",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/greek-core-list"
  },
